=begin
  go4invoker.lic -- keeps the invoker's spells up while bigshot hunts AFK.

  The invoker comes to Honeysuckle and Rose Avenue (room 3677) on Four Winds Isle at every
  even hour, game time (US Eastern), and leaves about 15 minutes later. From the logs: she
  thinks "...arriving ... in approximately 15 minutes" at :45, "...currently at Honeysuckle and
  Rose Avenue" at :00, was still answering at :08, and at :15 ASK got "Who are you trying to
  ask?". A spell-up costs 10,000 silver and lasts about 4 hours, so this goes at every other
  visit: when the last spell-up is at least 3.5 hours old by the time she arrives.

  What a visit looks like (all automatic, only when one is due and bigshot is running):
    * From 12 minutes before she arrives until 3 minutes after, a hunting bigshot is told to
      rest ($bigshot_should_rest). It finishes the fight, walks home and does its normal
      pre-rest chores. A bigshot that is already resting is simply caught there.
    * Once bigshot is resting in its resting room, it is paused. This waits for its rest
      chores (the profile's resting commands and scripts, and go2) to finish. Then, a minute
      before she arrives:
        - with less than 10,000 silver on hand: go2 bank (the bank nearest the resting room)
          and withdraw what's missing. Bank accounts are per town: on 11/10 Picko's withdraw
          at the Mist Harbor bank failed, so the money has to come from home first;
        - go2 3677 (go2 uses your FWI trinket both ways), wait for her, ASK her twice
          (the first ASK only quotes the price);
        - go2 back to the resting room, restart playsongs if it was playing, unpause bigshot.
    * If something goes wrong (no silver, she never showed, couldn't get there or back), a
      Discord line goes out through deadexit ($deadexit_notice), and bigshot is unpaused
      either way.

  Usage:
    ;go4invoker            watch and go when due (;afk on starts this, ;afk off stops it)
    ;go4invoker now        go right now and come back (she must be there or arriving within
                           15 minutes). Pauses bigshot for the trip if it's running.
    ;go4invoker status     last spell-up, next visit, whether that visit is due
    ;go4invoker done       record a spell-up you just got some other way

  While the watcher runs, Lich won't start a second copy, so `status`, `now` and `done` are for
  when it isn't running; `;afk` shows the watcher's status.

  The last spell-up time is UserVars.go4invoker_last. Any "You hand over your payment to ...
  invoker" line seen while this runs counts, including a trip you make by hand.

  Settings:
    ;vars set go4invoker_hours=3.5   how old the last spell-up must be (when she arrives)
                                     before going again

  Needs go2's FWI trinket setting (;go2 --fwi-trinket=<name>); without one the watcher says so
  and exits. On 11/12 Brayis, Htrowelzzif and Eepo had none set.
=end

module Go4Invoker
  module_function

  INVOKER_ROOM = 3677
  COST         = 10_000
  HOOK         = "go4invoker-hook"

  # Game text, from the saga logs (Salvi 11/11 10:00, Picko 11/10 08:04, Salvi 10/22 10:15).
  PRICE  = /The cost for my services is 10,000 silver/i
  PAID   = /You hand over your payment to .*invoker/i
  POOR   = /You do not have enough for my services/i
  ABSENT = /Who are you trying to ask\?/i
  WITHDRAW_RESULT = /hands you [\d,]+ silvers|already spent what you're trying to withdraw|don't have that much|promissory note|You have no account|insufficient/i

  # Tunables are methods so an edit applies on the next start (constants survive in Lich).
  # Minutes relative to her arrival (0 = she arrives, negative = before).
  def window_open;  -12; end   # start bringing bigshot home / catching it resting
  def force_until;    3; end   # last minute to tell a hunting bigshot to rest
  def leave_at;      -1; end   # leave the resting room for the island
  def last_leave;    10; end   # too late to start the trip after this
  def give_up_at;    14; end   # stop waiting for her / asking
  def poll_seconds;   5; end

  # Scripts that may be running in the resting room but never need waiting for.
  def never_wait_for; %w[playsongs rested timequit go4invoker]; end

  def say(msg)
    echo "[go4invoker] #{msg}"
  end

  # deadexit posts it to Discord with "[Name]" in front.
  def notice(text)
    $deadexit_notice = text
  end

  # ---- time -------------------------------------------------------------------

  # US Eastern time (game time) whatever this computer's zone is. DST runs from the second
  # Sunday of March 2:00 to the first Sunday of November 2:00.
  def eastern(t = Time.now)
    utc = t.getutc
    y = utc.year
    mar8 = Time.utc(y, 3, 8)
    dst_start = mar8 + ((7 - mar8.wday) % 7) * 86_400 + 7 * 3600
    nov1 = Time.utc(y, 11, 1)
    dst_end = nov1 + ((7 - nov1.wday) % 7) * 86_400 + 6 * 3600
    utc.getlocal((utc >= dst_start && utc < dst_end ? -4 : -5) * 3600)
  end

  # Minutes from her nearest visit: 0..59.99 after an even-hour arrival, -60..-0.01 before one.
  def rel_minutes(t = Time.now)
    e = eastern(t)
    m = (e.hour % 2) * 60 + e.min + e.sec / 60.0
    m >= 60 ? m - 120 : m
  end

  # Epoch second of the arrival rel_minutes is measured from.
  def visit_epoch(t = Time.now)
    ((t.to_f - rel_minutes(t) * 60) / 60.0).round * 60
  end

  def clock(epoch)
    eastern(Time.at(epoch)).strftime("%H:%M")
  end

  def ago(seconds)
    s = seconds.to_i
    s.negative? ? "just now" : format("%dh%02dm ago", s / 3600, (s % 3600) / 60)
  end

  # ---- the 4-hour clock ---------------------------------------------------------

  def refresh_seconds
    h = UserVars['go4invoker_hours'].to_s.strip.to_f
    h = 3.5 unless h.positive?
    (h * 3600).to_i
  end

  def last_spellup
    v = UserVars['go4invoker_last']
    v.to_s =~ /\A\d+\z/ ? v.to_i : nil
  end

  def record_spellup(at = Time.now.to_i)
    UserVars['go4invoker_last'] = at.to_i
  end

  def due_for?(visit)
    last = last_spellup
    last.nil? || visit - last >= refresh_seconds
  end

  # The first visit (this one if it's still on, else the next) that is due.
  def next_due_visit(t = Time.now)
    v = visit_epoch(t)
    v += 7200 if rel_minutes(t) > last_leave
    v += 7200 until due_for?(v)
    v
  end

  def status_line
    last = last_spellup
    nxt = next_due_visit
    "last spell-up #{last ? "#{ago(Time.now.to_i - last)} (#{clock(last)})" : 'unknown'}; " \
      "next trip at the #{clock(nxt)} visit (every #{(refresh_seconds / 3600.0).round(2)} h)"
  end

  # Any spell-up counts, a manual one included. The hook only sets a global; the main loop saves it.
  def install_hook
    DownstreamHook.remove(HOOK) rescue nil
    DownstreamHook.add(HOOK, proc { |line|
      begin
        $go4invoker_paid_at = Time.now.to_i if line =~ PAID
      rescue StandardError
        nil
      end
      line
    })
  end

  def remove_hook
    DownstreamHook.remove(HOOK) rescue nil
  end

  def save_paid
    at = $go4invoker_paid_at
    return unless at

    $go4invoker_paid_at = nil
    record_spellup(at)
  end

  # ---- where things are -----------------------------------------------------------

  def op
    v = UserVars['op']
    v.is_a?(Hash) ? v : {}
  end

  def resting_room
    id = op['resting_room_id'].to_s.strip
    id =~ /\A\d+\z/ ? id.to_i : nil
  end

  def room_id
    Room.current&.id
  rescue StandardError
    nil
  end

  # go2 only gets to Four Winds with the trinket (every mapped way onto the isle is a
  # trinket teleport). No path search here: one that never finds 3677 walks the whole map.
  def fwi_trinket
    UserVars['mapdb_fwi_trinket'].to_s.strip
  end

  def invoker_here?
    (Array(GameObj.npcs) + Array(GameObj.loot)).any? { |o| o.noun.to_s =~ /\Ainvoker\z/i || o.name.to_s =~ /\binvoker\b/i }
  rescue StandardError
    false
  end

  def go(target)
    Script.run("go2", "#{target} --disable-confirm", { quiet: true })
  end

  # ---- bigshot --------------------------------------------------------------------

  def bigshot?
    Script.running?("bigshot")
  end

  def resting_at_home?
    home = resting_room
    !home.nil? && $bigshot_status == :resting && room_id == home
  end

  # Scripts bigshot runs and waits on around a rest: the profile's "script X" resting and
  # hunting-prep commands, its resting scripts, and go2. Prep is in there because bigshot can
  # turn from resting to gearing up in the instant between the check and the pause.
  def rest_chores
    cmds = (Array(op['resting_commands']) + Array(op['hunting_prep_commands'])).join(',').split(',').map(&:strip)
    named = cmds.filter_map { |c| c[/\Ascript\s+(\S+)/i, 1] }
    named += Array(op['resting_scripts']).join(',').split(',').filter_map { |s| s.strip.split(/\s+/).first }
    (named + %w[go2]).uniq(&:downcase).reject { |n| never_wait_for.any? { |x| x.casecmp?(n) } }
  end

  def busy_chores
    rest_chores.select { |n| Script.running?(n) }
  end

  def pause_bigshot
    return false unless bigshot? && !Script.paused?("bigshot")

    Script.pause("bigshot")
    @paused_bigshot = true
  end

  def unpause_bigshot
    return unless @paused_bigshot

    @paused_bigshot = false
    Script.unpause("bigshot") if Script.running?("bigshot") && Script.paused?("bigshot")
  end

  # ---- music ----------------------------------------------------------------------

  # Stops playsongs (its before_dying stows the instrument) and returns its arguments for the restart.
  def stop_music
    s = Script.running.find { |x| x.name.to_s.casecmp?("playsongs") }
    return nil unless s

    args = s.vars[0].to_s
    Script.kill("playsongs")
    deadline = Time.now + 15
    sleep 0.2 while Script.running?("playsongs") && Time.now < deadline
    args
  end

  def restart_music(args)
    return if args.nil? || Script.running?("playsongs")

    args.strip.empty? ? Script.start("playsongs") : Script.start("playsongs", args)
  end

  # ---- the trip -------------------------------------------------------------------

  def silver_on_hand
    Lich::Util.silver_count.to_i
  rescue StandardError
    0
  end

  # Have 10,000 silver in hand, from the bank nearest to where we stand. Returns true/false.
  def ensure_silver
    have = silver_on_hand
    return true if have >= COST

    need = COST - have
    go("bank")
    waitrt?
    line = dothistimeout("withdraw #{need} silver", 6, WITHDRAW_RESULT).to_s
    have = silver_on_hand
    return true if have >= COST

    say "only #{have} silver after the withdraw (the teller said: #{line.strip[0, 120].inspect})."
    false
  end

  # Returns :paid, :poor, :absent or :no_answer.
  def ask_invoker
    2.times do
      waitrt?
      line = dothistimeout("ask invoker for spells", 5, Regexp.union(PRICE, PAID, POOR, ABSENT)).to_s
      if line =~ PAID
        record_spellup
        $go4invoker_paid_at = nil
        return :paid
      end
      return :poor if line =~ POOR
      return :absent if line =~ ABSENT
      return :no_answer unless line =~ PRICE
    end
    :no_answer
  end

  # Standing in 3677: wait for her to show, then ask. Asks blind every 20 s from her arrival time
  # on, in case she doesn't show up in the room objects.
  def get_spells
    next_probe = Time.now
    loop do
      r = rel_minutes
      if invoker_here? || (r >= 0 && Time.now >= next_probe)
        result = ask_invoker
        return result unless result == :absent

        next_probe = Time.now + 20
      end
      return :absent if r >= give_up_at || r < -20

      sleep 1
    end
  end

  # Bank if needed, island, spells, home. Returns :paid, :poor, :no_silver, :absent,
  # :no_answer or :unreachable.
  def trip
    home = room_id
    music = stop_music
    result = nil
    begin
      waitrt?
      waitcastrt?
      unless ensure_silver
        result = :no_silver
        return result
      end
      go(INVOKER_ROOM)
      if room_id != INVOKER_ROOM
        go(INVOKER_ROOM) # one retry: go2 sometimes stops after a teleport
      end
      if room_id != INVOKER_ROOM
        result = :unreachable
        return result
      end
      result = get_spells
    ensure
      if home && room_id != home
        go(home)
        go(home) if room_id != home
      end
      back = home.nil? || room_id == home
      say "!! couldn't get back to room #{home} (in #{room_id.inspect})." unless back
      notice("go4invoker could not get back to room #{home} after the invoker trip (now in #{room_id.inspect}).") unless back
      restart_music(music) if back
    end
    result
  end

  def report(result, visit)
    case result
    when :paid
      say "spelled up. #{status_line}."
    when :no_silver
      notice("invoker trip skipped: couldn't get 10,000 silver from the bank (#{clock(visit)} visit).")
      say "!! couldn't get 10,000 silver -- no spells this visit."
    when :poor
      notice("the invoker said I didn't have enough silver (#{clock(visit)} visit).")
      say "!! she said you don't have enough silver."
    when :absent
      notice("the invoker never showed at Honeysuckle and Rose Avenue (#{clock(visit)} visit).")
      say "!! she never showed by #{give_up_at} past the hour."
    when :unreachable
      notice("go4invoker couldn't get to room #{INVOKER_ROOM} (FWI trinket?) for the #{clock(visit)} visit.")
      say "!! couldn't get to room #{INVOKER_ROOM}. Is go2's FWI trinket set (;go2 --fwi-trinket=<name>)?"
    else
      notice("the invoker didn't answer (#{clock(visit)} visit).")
      say "!! no answer from the invoker."
    end
  end

  # bigshot is resting at home inside the window: hold it, let the chores finish, go.
  def run_visit(visit)
    pause_bigshot
    say "holding bigshot for the invoker's #{clock(visit)} visit."
    said = false
    until (busy = busy_chores).empty?
      if rel_minutes > last_leave
        say "rest chores (#{busy.join(', ')}) still running at #{last_leave} past -- skipping this visit."
        notice("invoker trip skipped: bigshot's rest chores (#{busy.join(', ')}) ran past #{clock(visit + last_leave * 60)}.")
        return :late
      end
      say "waiting for #{busy.join(', ')} to finish." unless said
      said = true
      sleep 1
    end
    sleep 1 while rel_minutes < leave_at
    result = trip
    report(result, visit)
    result
  ensure
    unpause_bigshot
  end

  # One poll of the watcher. Returns a symbol saying what it did (for tests).
  def tick(now = Time.now)
    save_paid
    visit = visit_epoch(now)
    r = rel_minutes(now)
    return :outside if r < window_open || r > last_leave
    return :not_due unless due_for?(visit)
    return :handled if @handled_visit == visit
    return :no_bigshot unless bigshot?
    return :bigshot_paused if Script.paused?("bigshot") # someone else (deader, disarmguard) paused it
    return :no_resting_room if resting_room.nil?

    if resting_at_home?
      @handled_visit = visit
      run_visit(visit)
      return :visited
    end
    return :resting_elsewhere if $bigshot_status == :resting # on its way home
    return :too_late_to_force if r > force_until
    return :forced if @forced_visit == visit

    @forced_visit = visit
    $rest_reason = "invoker spell-up." if $rest_reason.to_s.strip.empty?
    $bigshot_should_rest = true
    say "the invoker arrives at #{clock(visit)} -- sending bigshot home to rest first."
    :force_rest
  end

  def watch
    if fwi_trinket.empty?
      say "go2 has no FWI trinket for #{Char.name}, so it can't get to the invoker on Four Winds Isle. " \
          "Set one with ;go2 --fwi-trinket=<name> and start this again. Exiting."
      return
    end
    say "watching. #{status_line}."
    loop do
      exit if checkdead
      begin
        tick
      rescue StandardError => e
        say "error: #{e.class} #{e.message}"
        unpause_bigshot
      end
      $go4invoker_status = status_line
      sleep poll_seconds
    end
  end

  def now_command
    if fwi_trinket.empty?
      say "go2 has no FWI trinket for #{Char.name} (;go2 --fwi-trinket=<name>), so it can't get to Four Winds Isle."
      return
    end
    r = rel_minutes
    visit = visit_epoch
    if r >= give_up_at || r < -15
      nxt = visit + (r >= 0 ? 7200 : 0)
      say "she isn't there now; next visit at #{clock(nxt)}."
      return
    end
    pause_bigshot
    begin
      waitrt?
      result = trip
      report(result, visit)
    ensure
      unpause_bigshot
    end
  end

  def run(arg)
    @paused_bigshot = false
    @handled_visit = nil
    @forced_visit = nil
    $go4invoker_paid_at = nil
    case arg.to_s.strip.downcase
    when ""
      install_hook
      watch
    when "now"
      install_hook
      now_command
      save_paid
    when "status"
      say status_line
      say "bigshot #{bigshot? ? 'running' : 'not running'}; resting room #{resting_room.inspect}; " \
          "FWI trinket #{UserVars['mapdb_fwi_trinket'].inspect}"
    when "done"
      record_spellup
      say "recorded a spell-up now. #{status_line}."
    else
      say "Unknown option '#{arg}'. Use ;go4invoker, ;go4invoker now, ;go4invoker status or ;go4invoker done."
    end
  end
end

before_dying do
  Go4Invoker.unpause_bigshot
  Go4Invoker.remove_hook
  Go4Invoker.save_paid
  $go4invoker_status = nil
end

Go4Invoker.run(Script.current.vars[1])
